    "q-148315": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148315",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{7}{4},$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{5}{2},$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\frac{3}{4}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{5}{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
