    "q-148330": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148330",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.24,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.06,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.08.$ Find $\\text{Var}[2X-8Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-8Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 0.24+(-8)^{2}\\cdot 0.06+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-8)\\cdot 0.08 \\\\  & =0.96+3.84-2.56 \\\\  & =2.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
