    "q-148160": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148160",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "For three random variables ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3},$ we have the following variances and covariances:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]=5,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]=4,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}]=2\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]=3,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]=1,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]=2\\,\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+4{X}_{3}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},…,{X}_{n}$ are random variables, and ${a}_{1},…,{a}_{n}$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{X}_{i}]={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{i}]+2{\\sum }_{i<j}{a}_{i}{a}_{j}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{i},{X}_{j}].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+4{X}_{3}] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 4+{4}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =45+16+32+36+24+32 \\\\  & =185.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
